              { label: '3. Hard data', body: 'A classic method computes self-similarity <code>S(i,j)=sim(F(i),F(j))</code> and a novelty curve by checkerboard convolution. Peaks in <code>novelty(t)</code> above threshold are boundary candidates.' },
